From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:12:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: Keep the RK3528's aclk pre auto gating
 off

The RK3528's aclk pre auto gating stops aclk while the VOP idles, which
takes the registers of its IOMMU with it: no read of them completes, and
the CPU locks up. The Rockchip BSP turns it off before it attaches the
IOMMU; do so before the attach that enables it.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c | 8 ++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
index fba7703..60c0ce5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
@@ -890,6 +890,14 @@ static int vop2_enable(struct vop2 *vop2)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_pm;
 
+	/*
+	 * The RK3528's aclk pre auto gating stops aclk while the VOP idles,
+	 * and the registers of its IOMMU with it: no read of them completes.
+	 */
+	if (vop2->version == VOP_VERSION_RK3528)
+		regmap_clear_bits(vop2->map, RK3568_SYS_AUTO_GATING_CTRL,
+				  RK3528_SYS_AUTO_GATING_CTRL__ACLK_PRE_AUTO_GATING_EN);
+
 	ret = rockchip_drm_dma_attach_device(vop2->drm, vop2->dev);
 	if (ret) {
 		drm_err(vop2->drm, "failed to attach dma mapping, %d\n", ret);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.h
index d822bcf..78e0040 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.h
@@ -775,6 +775,7 @@ enum dst_factor_mode {
 #define RK3568_VP0_MIPI_CTRL__DCLK_DIV2			BIT(4)
 
 #define RK3568_SYS_AUTO_GATING_CTRL__AUTO_GATING_EN	BIT(31)
+#define RK3528_SYS_AUTO_GATING_CTRL__ACLK_PRE_AUTO_GATING_EN	BIT(7)
 
 #define RK3568_DSP_IF_POL__CFG_DONE_IMD			BIT(28)
 
